# Generated data for 2021-12-set2
SUBPARTS = [{'id': '2021-12-set2-conv-1', 'subpart_code': 'conv-1', 'section_id': '2021-12-set2-sec-a', 'section_title': 'Section A: Long Conversations', 'type': 'conversation', 'title': 'Conversation 1 · 环保活动家新书《超越回收》争议与温和环保理念倡导', 'topic_zh': '环保活动家新书《超越回收》争议与温和环保理念倡导', 'question_range': 'Q1 ~ Q4', 'questions': [1, 2, 3, 4], 'sp_start': 48.0, 'sp_end': 184.0, 'sentences': [('M', 'Good morning and welcome to People in the News.', '早上好，欢迎收听《新闻人物》节目。'), ('M', 'With me today is Meghan Brown, an environmental activist whose controversial new book Beyond Recycling is making headlines.', '今天来到我们演播室的是梅根·布朗，她是一位环保活动家，其引发热议的新书《超越回收》近日登上了各大新闻头条。'), ('W', 'Hi, Brian. Thanks for having me today.', '嗨，布莱恩。谢谢你今天的邀请。'), ('W', "I'm excited to explain to the audience what my book is really about.", '我非常激动能向广大听众朋友们深入阐释我这本新书的真正核心要义。'), ('M', "Critics of your book assert that you're trying to force radical changes on the entire country.", '针对你新书的批评者们断言，你正企图将激进的剧烈变革强加给整个国家。'), ('M', 'Some claim that you want to force everyone to eat a vegetarian diet and make private transport illegal.', '有人甚至声称你企图强制所有人改吃纯素食，并宣布私人交通出行违法。'), ('W', "I'm aware of those claims, but they simply aren't true.", '我注意到了这些甚嚣尘上的言论，但它们根本不是事实。'), ('W', "People who haven't read the book are making assumptions about my arguments.", '那些压根没读过这本书的人正在对我书中的论点妄加揣测。'), ('W', "They know I'm a vegetarian, that I don't wear leather or fur, and that I always use public transportation.", '他们只知道我个人茹素、从不穿皮草皮革，并且出行始终坚持乘坐公共交通工具。'), ('W', "So they're depicting me as a radical animal rights activist and environmentalist determined to force my beliefs on others.", '于是他们就把我描绘成一个铁了心要把个人信仰强加于人的激进动物保护主义者和极端环保狂热分子。'), ('M', "But don't you want others to adopt your practices? You've campaigned for animal rights and the environment for decades.", '但难道你真的不希望其他人也效仿采纳你的生活方式吗？毕竟你数十年来一直在为动物权利与环境保护奔走呼吁。'), ('W', "I'd love it if people choose to live as I do.", '如果大家自愿选择像我这样生活，我当然会由衷高兴。'), ('W', 'But my life choices are based on my personal convictions.', '但我个人的生活抉择是建立在自己内心的坚定信念之上的。'), ('W', "They aren't my recommendations for others who don't share those convictions.", '对于那些并不认同这些信念的人，我绝不会以此去苛求命令他们。'), ('M', 'Well, in this excerpt from your book, you argue that meat consumption and private transport are devastating the environment and that the best choices for the planet are vegetarian diets and public transport.', '可是在你书中的这一节选段落里，你明确主张肉类消费和私家车出行正在毁灭地球生态，而对地球最好的选择就是素食与公共交通。'), ('W', "I did write that. But those are examples of what I call best practices, not what I'm actually suggesting.", '我确实写过这些文字，但这只是我所定义的最优示范案例，并非我向公众提出的实际操作要求。'), ('W', 'In my guidelines for saving the environment, I suggest modest changes, like eating vegetarian meals two days a week.', '在我为拯救环境所拟定的践行指南中，我建议的是温和适度的改变，比如每周吃两天素食。'), ('M', 'You also endorse high taxes on meat and other animal products and increased taxes on gasoline. Those taxes could force poor people to adopt your life choices.', '你还主张对肉类及其他动物制品征收重税，并大幅提高汽油税，这些税负可能会逼迫贫困人群不得不被迫接受你的生活方式。'), ('W', "But the taxes I suggest aren't that high, less than 3% only.", '但我所提议的税率并不高，仅仅不到百分之三。'), ('W', 'Plus, the money generated would be allocated to environmental protection, which benefits everyone.', '况且，筹集到的所有税收资金都将专项用于环境保护，而良好的环境将使每一个人都普遍受益。')]}, {'id': '2021-12-set2-conv-2', 'subpart_code': 'conv-2', 'section_id': '2021-12-set2-sec-a', 'section_title': 'Section A: Long Conversations', 'type': 'conversation', 'title': 'Conversation 2 · 畅销书《成功秘诀》探讨成功者特质与职场激情培育环境', 'topic_zh': '畅销书《成功秘诀》探讨成功者特质与职场激情培育环境', 'question_range': 'Q5 ~ Q8', 'questions': [5, 6, 7, 8], 'sp_start': 257.0, 'sp_end': 391.0, 'sentences': [('M', 'With me in the studio today is Ms. Jane Logan, author of a new book, Secrets to Success.', '今天做客演播室的是简·洛根女士，她是新书《成功的秘诀》的作者。'), ('M', 'She claims to have uncovered how people achieve success.', '她自称揭开了人们究竟是如何取得成功的奥秘。'), ('M', 'So Ms. Logan, in your book, you claim that successful people have many things in common. For instance, they know their strengths when pursuing a goal.', '那么洛根女士，在你的书中，你指出成功人士有着许多惊人的共同点，比如他们在追求目标时深谙自身的长处与优势所在。'), ('W', "That's right.", '确实如此。'), ('W', 'They also tend to be motivated by a negative or positive life event.', '他们也往往容易受到人生中某次或消极挫折、或积极正向的大事件的强烈驱使。'), ('W', 'They credit their success to having someone in their life who believes in them.', '而且他们常将自己的成功归功于生命中有一位由衷信任并看好他们的人。'), ('M', 'You also write that there are a number of different factors related to success. And while successful people are driven to achieve their goals, the ultra successful have even greater ambition.', '你还写到与成功相关的诸多不同要素；虽然成功人士都极具达成目标的内驱力，但那些登峰造极的超级成功者往往拥有更为宏大的远大抱负。'), ('W', 'Yes, greater ambition as well as a burning desire to be the best of the best is also a common characteristic.', '是的，更为宏伟的雄心抱负，以及一种渴望成为出类拔萃者中之最强者的炽热愿望，同样是普遍特征。'), ('M', "Right. So those who are determined don't see obstacles as something that prevents success, but mere inconveniences that need to be overcome.", '没错。因此那些意志坚定的人绝不把障碍视作阻碍成功的绊脚石，而仅仅是必须被克服的些许不便而已。'), ('W', 'Absolutely.', '完全正确。'), ('W', 'Successful people are also optimistic as it is important to stay positive while being aware of obstacles that can deter us from achieving our goals.', '成功人士同时非常乐观，因为在清醒洞察可能阻碍达成目标的障碍之余，始终保持积极乐观的心态至关重要。'), ('M', "That's a good point. All too often, people give up at the first hurdle. Would you say then that most successful people make it all by themselves?", '说得真好。太多人往往在第一道难关前就半途而废了。那么你会认为大多数成功者都是单打独斗全靠自己取得成功的吗？'), ('W', 'Not exactly. They are usually good at cooperating with people and understanding the needs of others.', '并不尽然。他们通常极擅长与人协作，并深刻理解他人的真实诉求。'), ('M', 'So people will be willing to help them, I guess.', '所以我猜想大家也都会非常乐意向他们伸出援手。'), ('W', "That's correct. And this often leads to a great deal of mutual respect, whether it's with a colleague, an assistant or even a receptionist.", '正是如此。这也往往会促成深厚的彼此相互尊重，无论对方是同事、助手还是前台接待员。'), ('M', 'Most successful people I know are very passionate about their work. Would you say that passion is the single biggest key to success?', '我认识的大多数成功人士对自己的事业都倾注了极大的热情与激情。你会认为激情是通向成功的最关键单一钥匙吗？'), ('W', 'Not entirely.', '不完全是。'), ('W', "There's a prerequisite, that is, you have to work in an environment that nurtures passion.", '这其中存在一个先决条件：那就是你必须置身于一个能够滋养与催生激情的环境之中。'), ('W', 'If that exists, success will follow.', '若具备这一土壤，成功便会水到渠成。')]}, {'id': '2021-12-set2-pass-1', 'subpart_code': 'pass-1', 'section_id': '2021-12-set2-sec-b', 'section_title': 'Section B: Passages', 'type': 'passage', 'title': 'Passage 1 · 巨型蝙蝠与微型蝙蝠感知机理及生态适应特征', 'topic_zh': '巨型蝙蝠与微型蝙蝠感知机理及生态适应特征', 'question_range': 'Q9 ~ Q11', 'questions': [9, 10, 11], 'sp_start': 490.0, 'sp_end': 610.0, 'sentences': [('Speaker', "The saying 'blind as a bat' simply isn't correct.", '俗语所说的“像蝙蝠一样瞎”根本站不住脚。'), ('Speaker', 'The truth is that all 1,100 bat species can see and often their vision is pretty good, although not as excellent as other night-hunting animals.', '事实的真相是，所有1100种蝙蝠都具备视力，且视力往往相当不错，尽管可能不及其他夜行捕食动物那般敏锐卓越。'), ('Speaker', 'There are two main groups of bats, which are believed to have evolved independently of each other, but both from a common ancestor.', '蝙蝠主要分为两大类群，学界认为它们虽然起源于共同的古老祖先，但在进化轨迹上各自独立演变。'), ('Speaker', 'The first group, known as the mega bats, are mostly medium-sized or large bats who eat fruits, flowers, and sometimes small animals or fish.', '第一大类被称为“大蝙蝠”（巨型蝠），大多属于体型中等或偏大的蝠类，主要以水果、花蜜为食，偶尔也会捕食小动物或小鱼。'), ('Speaker', 'These species have distinctive visual centers and big eyes.', '这类物种拥有极其发达独特的视觉中枢和硕大醒目的眼睛。'), ('Speaker', 'They use senses of vision and smell to capture their prey.', '它们主要凭借敏锐的视觉与嗅觉来搜寻并锁定猎物。'), ('Speaker', 'For example, Flying Foxes not only see well during daylight, but can also distinguish colors.', '例如狐蝠不仅在白昼拥有绝佳视力，甚至还能敏锐辨识各种色彩。'), ('Speaker', 'They actually rely on their daylight vision and cannot fly during the night with no moonlight.', '它们在生理上高度依赖昼光视力，在没有月光的漆黑夜晚甚至完全无法展翅飞行。'), ('Speaker', 'The second group, called micro bats, are smaller in size and mostly eat insects.', '第二大类被称为“小蝙蝠”（微型蝠），体型相对娇小，主要以捕食昆虫为生。'), ('Speaker', 'These species use echolocation to find their way and identify food.', '这类物种主要依靠高超的回声定位系统来探测航向与精准辨别猎物食物。'), ('Speaker', 'Scientists have proven that despite their poorly developed small eyes, these bats still can see during the day.', '科学家们已经证实，尽管它们的小眼睛发育相对退化，但在白天依然具有基础的视物能力。'), ('Speaker', 'When we consider the nightly lifestyle of these bats, we will see they have to be sensitive to the changing light levels because this is how they sense when to start hunting.', '当我们审视这些小蝙蝠昼伏夜出的生活习性时便会发现，它们必须对外界光照强度的微妙变化保持敏感，因为这正是它们感知何时出巢觅食的天然节律信号。'), ('Speaker', 'Moreover, vision is used by micro bats to travel over long distances, beyond the range of echolocation.', '此外，小蝙蝠在进行远距离迁徙飞行时，在超出回声定位探测范围的广袤空间里，同样需要依靠视觉来导航。'), ('Speaker', 'So the truth is, there are no bats which are naturally blind.', '因此真相是：世界上根本不存在任何天生失明的蝙蝠。'), ('Speaker', 'Some species use their sense of hearing more than their eyes as a matter of adaptation to a particular lifestyle, but their eyes are still functional.', '某些蝙蝠物种之所以侧重使用听觉远甚于视觉，纯粹是为了适应其独特的生存方式而演化出的特化适应，但它们的双眼依然完好具备视觉功能。')]}, {'id': '2021-12-set2-pass-2', 'subpart_code': 'pass-2', 'section_id': '2021-12-set2-sec-b', 'section_title': 'Section B: Passages', 'type': 'passage', 'title': 'Passage 2 · 少儿教育电视节目冲突情节对儿童攻击行为的负面影响及家长引导', 'topic_zh': '少儿教育电视节目冲突情节对儿童攻击行为的负面影响及家长引导', 'question_range': 'Q12 ~ Q15', 'questions': [12, 13, 14, 15], 'sp_start': 668.0, 'sp_end': 785.0, 'sentences': [('Speaker', "A study has found that educational TV shows come with an added lesson that influences the child's behavior.", '一项最新科学研究发现，少儿教育类电视节目往往伴生着一种会潜移默化影响孩子行为的额外附带效应。'), ('Speaker', 'Children spending more time watching educational programs increase their emotional aggression toward other children.', '花更多时间观看教育类节目的儿童，对同龄其他孩子表现出的情绪性攻击倾向反而显著增加。'), ('Speaker', 'This shows that children can learn the educational lesson that was intended.', '这表明孩子们固然能够吸收节目原本意图传达的正向教育教训。'), ('Speaker', "However, they're also learning other things along the way.", '然而，在潜移默化中，他们也同时顺带习得了其他不健康的举动。'), ('Speaker', 'This unintended impact has to do with the portrayal of conflict in media and how preschool-age children comprehend that conflict.', '这种始料未及的负面冲击，与媒体对矛盾冲突的刻画方式以及学龄前幼童解读冲突的认知机制息息相关。'), ('Speaker', 'TV and movie producers often incorporate an element of bad behavior.', '影视制作人在编排剧情时往往会刻意植入不良言行的负面戏剧元素。'), ('Speaker', 'This is to teach children a lesson at the end of the program.', '其初衷本是通过片尾的反转与警示来给孩子们上一堂生动的道德启蒙课。'), ('Speaker', 'Educational shows have pro-education and pro-social goals.', '少儿教育节目固然秉持着崇高的崇尚教育与亲社会行为目标。'), ('Speaker', 'However, conflict between characters is often depicted with characters being unkind to each other or they may use emotionally aggressive tactics with each other.', '但在具体呈现角色之间的摩擦时，人物往往被刻画得尖酸刻薄、互不相让，或者频繁施加情绪层面的言语攻击与敌视手段。'), ('Speaker', "Preschool children really don't get the moral of the story.", '学龄前幼儿根本无法参透整个故事的大团圆寓意与教化主旨。'), ('Speaker', "That's because it requires that they understand how all the parts of the show fit together.", '因为要领悟深层寓意，必须具备能够将整个剧情的前后起承转合融会贯通的逻辑思维。'), ('Speaker', 'You need pretty complicated cognitive skills and memory skills to be able to do that.', '做到这一点需要相当成熟复杂的认知整合能力与长时记忆能力。'), ('Speaker', 'These are still developing in young children.', '而这些关键心理技能在低龄儿童身上仍在发育演进阶段。'), ('Speaker', "However, parents shouldn't completely constrain children's viewing.", '然而，家长们大可不必因此就因噎废食，彻底剥夺禁止孩子观看此类节目。'), ('Speaker', 'Parents should instead watch with their kids and help them to understand the plot.', '相反，父母应当陪伴孩子共同观看，并在身旁耐心引导他们理解剧情脉络。'), ('Speaker', 'Parents can comment along the way and then explain the message at the end.', '家长可以在观看过程中适时点评探讨，并在节目收尾时为孩子点明升华核心寓意。'), ('Speaker', 'They should explain how certain types of behavior were not appropriate.', '父母应当向孩子明确指出某些冲动言行举止为何是不妥当、不体面的。'), ('Speaker', 'This will help children interpret and get the message and help them learn to watch the show for those messages.', '这能有效帮助孩子正确解读并领会正能量信息，教会他们如何带着批判思辨眼光从影视作品中汲取正面营养。')]}, {'id': '2021-12-set2-rec-1', 'subpart_code': 'rec-1', 'section_id': '2021-12-set2-sec-c', 'section_title': 'Section C: Recordings', 'type': 'recording', 'title': 'Recording 1 · 居家进门脱鞋倡议：鞋底细菌传播、地板磨损与室内空气污染', 'topic_zh': '居家进门脱鞋倡议：鞋底细菌传播、地板磨损与室内空气污染', 'question_range': 'Q16 ~ Q18', 'questions': [16, 17, 18], 'sp_start': 889.0, 'sp_end': 1045.0, 'sentences': [('Speaker', 'While it has long been a practice in Asian countries, many people in Western countries have yet to embrace the no-shoes-in-the-house rule.', '进门脱鞋虽然在亚洲国家由来已久、蔚然成风，但许多西方国家的人们至今仍未普及这一习惯。'), ('Speaker', 'For many in those countries, wiping their shoes before going inside is regarded as sufficient.', '在这些国家，很多人认为只要进门前在脚垫上蹭蹭鞋底就完全足够了。'), ('Speaker', "After all, they may think a little dirt doesn't hurt anyone.", '毕竟在他们潜意识里，带进门的一丁点泥土污垢无伤大雅，伤不到任何人。'), ('Speaker', 'But I can give you several good reasons why people should remove their shoes before going inside their homes.', '但我今天可以列举出几个强有力的充分理由，证明大家踏入家门前必须脱鞋。'), ('Speaker', 'Bacteria are everywhere.', '细菌在自然界中无孔不入。'), ('Speaker', 'They collect on your shoes when you walk along sidewalks, public toilet floors and even office carpets.', '当你在人行道、公共卫生间地面乃至办公室地毯上行走漫步时，海量细菌便附着聚集在你的鞋底。'), ('Speaker', 'In one study conducted at an American university, researchers collected microscopic germs from footwear.', '在美国一所知名大学开展的一项专项科研中，研究人员从各样鞋底采集了显微病菌样本。'), ('Speaker', 'They found that up to 421,000 units of bacteria can collect on the outside of a single shoe.', '他们惊人地发现，仅凭单只鞋子的外部外侧，就可积聚高达42.1万个单位的密集细菌！'), ('Speaker', 'And it only takes a little bit of dirt to damage your timber floors.', '而且只需带进微量的细小砂石尘土，就足以划伤损坏你昂贵的实木地板。'), ('Speaker', "The more dirt you track in, the more it scratches and the more often you'd have to clean.", '你踩进屋内的泥沙越多，地板被刮擦受损的痕迹就越密，清洁打理的频率也随之激增。'), ('Speaker', 'The extra scrubbing will harm your floors over time.', '日积月累频繁过度地擦洗磨损，久而久之必然重创实木地板的寿命与光泽。'), ('Speaker', 'Shoes can also leave marks and scratches on floors, especially high heels or shoes with pointed or hard parts.', '鞋子还会在地板上留下触目的压痕与划痕，尤其是细高跟鞋或带有尖锐硬质部件的硬底鞋。'), ('Speaker', 'These can dent and scratch your floor.', '这些硬鞋极易把地板砸出凹坑、划出深沟。'), ('Speaker', 'And if you live in an apartment building, removing your noisy shoes is the polite thing to do out of consideration for your downstairs neighbors.', '此外如果你居住在公寓楼里，脱下咚咚作响的硬底鞋，是对楼下邻居体贴周到的基本现代文明礼貌。'), ('Speaker', 'Walking around with bare feet is actually better for your feet.', '在室内赤足行走对你的双脚健康大有裨益。'), ('Speaker', 'It strengthens the muscles in your feet.', '光脚行走能够充分锻炼强化足底及足弓各处肌肉群。'), ('Speaker', 'Though many people are accustomed to wearing shoes during all their waking hours, the more time you spend wearing shoes, the more likely you are to incur foot injuries as a result.', '尽管许多人习惯于在清醒的全部时间内都穿着鞋，但穿鞋时长越长，罹患各类足部劳损病痛的风险其实越高。'), ('Speaker', "And if people aren't yet convinced by my arguments, I can give one final reason.", '如果大家听到这里仍对我的论点将信将疑，我还可以抛出最后一个决定性的硬核理由。'), ('Speaker', 'The dust and toxic chemicals you bring into your house via your shoes can deteriorate the air quality in your home.', '你通过鞋底从户外带入室内的粉尘与有毒化学残留物，会严重恶化家中的空气质量。'), ('Speaker', 'Toxic chemicals are everywhere in our lives: insect-killing chemicals used on public grass areas, cleaning chemicals on the floors of public areas.', '有毒化学品在现代城市生活中几乎无处不在：喷洒在公共草坪上的杀虫剂灭草剂、公共场所地面上残留的强力工业清洁溶剂等。'), ('Speaker', 'By kicking off your shoes before you enter the home, you are denying entry to these harmful chemicals.', '只要你在踏入家门前脱掉鞋子，你便将这些致命的有害化学品统统拒之门外。'), ('Speaker', 'Given the amount of time we spend in classrooms, and the number of shoes that pass through them every day, you may well understand me if I were to propose a no-shoes-in-the-classroom rule.', '鉴于我们在教室里共度了如此漫长的时光、每天穿梭其中的鞋子如此之多，如果我提议在教室内也推行脱鞋制度，大家想必也完全能够感同身受了吧。')]}, {'id': '2021-12-set2-rec-2', 'subpart_code': 'rec-2', 'section_id': '2021-12-set2-sec-c', 'section_title': 'Section C: Recordings', 'type': 'recording', 'title': 'Recording 2 · 情绪心理机制、原始大脑与理性认知接纳及应对之道', 'topic_zh': '情绪心理机制、原始大脑与理性认知接纳及应对之道', 'question_range': 'Q19 ~ Q21', 'questions': [19, 20, 21], 'sp_start': 1109.0, 'sp_end': 1280.0, 'sentences': [('Speaker', 'Emotions are an essential and inseparable part of our consciousness.', '情绪是我们人类精神意识中不可或缺且密不可分的核心组成部分。'), ('Speaker', 'They are part of a built-in mechanism, which allows us to cope with the ups and downs of our lives both physically and mentally.', '它们是机体自带的内置防御调节机制，让我们在生理与心理上得以抵御应对人生的起伏跌宕。'), ('Speaker', 'When we hide our emotions and our true feelings, we stop being genuine, spontaneous and authentic in our relationships.', '当我们刻意掩饰自己的情绪与真实感受时，我们在人际交往中便丧失了真诚、自发与真实。'), ('Speaker', 'When we put on cultivated and polished faces in the company of others, we stop being true to ourselves.', '当我们在人群中强行戴上精心修饰的虚伪面具时，我们便背叛了真实的自我。'), ('Speaker', 'Socially, it may be a good tactic to hide our true emotions, but morally it is also a breach of faith and trust.', '在社交层面，隐藏真实情绪或许是一套圆滑体面的策略，但从道德诚信层面而言，这无疑是对真诚与信任的违背。'), ('Speaker', 'Although humans are more advanced and intelligent, animals are more genuine and authentic in their behavior and responses than human beings.', '虽然人类拥有高度智慧与文明进化，但动物在行为与情感反应上却往往比人类要真实纯粹得多。'), ('Speaker', 'The more educated we are, the less transparent and reliable we become.', '有时我们受的社会化教育程度越高，内心的透明度与可信度反而越发大打折扣。'), ('Speaker', 'We are drawn to our pets because pets do not lie.', '我们之所以深深迷恋宠物，正是因为宠物永远不会撒谎。'), ('Speaker', 'One of the first steps in dealing with emotions such as anger or fear is to acknowledge them as normal and human.', '应对愤怒或恐惧等负面情绪的第一步，便是坦然承认它们是人类正常而健全的人性本能。'), ('Speaker', 'There is nothing sinful or immoral about being emotional, unless your emotions make you inhuman, insensitive and cruel to others.', '产生情绪起伏本身绝非罪恶或不道德之事，除非你的情绪失控使你变得丧失人性、麻木不仁并对他人施加残忍。'), ('Speaker', 'Feelings of guilt associated with emotions are more devastating and damaging than the experience of emotion itself.', '伴随情绪而来的自责与负罪感，往往比情绪本身的冲击体验更具破坏力与杀伤力。'), ('Speaker', 'So when you deal with the problem of emotions, you should learn not only how to control them but also how to accept them and manage the guilt and anguish arising from them.', '因此在直面情绪困扰时，你不仅要学会如何自制调控，更要懂得坦然接纳它们，并化解因情绪而生的愧疚与痛苦。'), ('Speaker', 'Our brains are made up of a primitive inner core and a more evolved and rational outer core.', '我们的大脑由原始的古老内核以及后天高度进化的理性外皮层共同构成。'), ('Speaker', 'Most of the time, the rational part of the mind controls the information coming from the primitive core and makes its own decisions as to what to do and how to respond.', '在绝大多数日常时刻，理智的大脑外层能够有效把控来自原始内核的神经信号，自主决策该采取何种行为与得体反应。'), ('Speaker', 'However, during critical situations, especially when a threat is perceived, the outer core loses control and fails to regulate the impulses and instinctual responses coming from the primitive brain.', '然而在遭遇危急时刻、尤其是感知到外界重大威胁时，理性外皮层会瞬间失控，难以遏制来自原始大脑的本能冲动与应激反应。'), ('Speaker', 'As a result, we let disturbing thoughts and emotions arise in our consciousness and surrender to our primitive behavior.', '其结果便是我们任由困扰的思绪与狂暴的情绪在意识中激荡蔓延，彻底沦陷于原始的本能行为。'), ('Speaker', 'In times of emotional turmoil, remember that emotions arise because your senses are wired to the primitive part of your mind which is self-regulated, autonomous and spontaneous.', '在情绪遭遇狂风暴雨的动荡时刻，请牢记：情绪之所以骤起，是因为你的感官直连着自律、自主且高度自发的原始神经系统。'), ('Speaker', 'Your rational mind does not always deal with the messages coming from it effectively.', '你的理性心智并不总能高效妥善地处理原始中枢传递出的所有信号。'), ('Speaker', 'These messages are part of your survival mechanism and should not be stifled simply because emotions are unhealthy and betray your weaknesses.', '这些情感警报本就是你生存适应机制不可或缺的一环，切莫因盲目认定情绪是病态的或暴露脆弱而粗暴地将它们彻底扼杀扼灭。'), ('Speaker', 'When emotions arise, instead of stifling them, pay attention to them and try to understand the messages they are trying to deliver.', '当强烈情绪涌现时，与其强行压抑，不如去倾听关注它们，并尽力去理解它们背后企图传达给你的深层密码与警示。'), ('Speaker', 'This way you make use of your emotions without losing your balance and inner stability.', '如此一来，你便能借势驾驭情绪的力量，而不至于失控倾覆内心的平静与内在定力。')]}, {'id': '2021-12-set2-rec-3', 'subpart_code': 'rec-3', 'section_id': '2021-12-set2-sec-c', 'section_title': 'Section C: Recordings', 'type': 'recording', 'title': 'Recording 3 · 第二次绿色革命：全球粮食危机、低碳抗旱作物与农业科技投资', 'topic_zh': '第二次绿色革命：全球粮食危机、低碳抗旱作物与农业科技投资', 'question_range': 'Q22 ~ Q25', 'questions': [22, 23, 24, 25], 'sp_start': 1339.0, 'sp_end': 1540.0, 'sentences': [('Speaker', 'Good morning, class. My topic today is how to feed a hungry world.', '大家早上好。我今天演讲的主题是《如何养活这个饥饿的世界》。'), ('Speaker', "The world's population is expected to grow from 6.8 billion today to 9.1 billion by 2050.", '全球总人口预计将从当今的68亿大幅飙升至2050年的91亿之巨。'), ('Speaker', "Meanwhile, the world's population more than doubled from 3 billion between 1961 and 2007.", '在此之前，在1961年至2007年间，世界人口已从30亿翻了一倍有余。'), ('Speaker', 'Simultaneously, food production has been constrained by a lack of scientific research.', '与此同步的是，全球粮食增产正受到农业前沿科研投入匮乏的严重制约。'), ('Speaker', "Still, the task of feeding the world's population in 2050 seems easily possible.", '然而，在2050年彻底养活全球庞大人口的宏伟任务，依然完全具有可行性。'), ('Speaker', 'What is needed is a second green revolution.', '当务之急是掀起一场划时代的“第二次绿色革命”。'), ('Speaker', 'This is an approach that is described as the sustainable growth of global agriculture.', '这是一套被定义为全球农业可持续集约化增长的科学路径。'), ('Speaker', 'Such a revolution will require a wholesale shift of priorities in agricultural research.', '这样一场深刻的农业变革，亟需全球农业科研优先事项发生翻天覆地的全面转向。'), ('Speaker', 'There is an urgent need for new crop varieties.', '当前最迫切的需求便是培育革新性的农作物新品种。'), ('Speaker', 'They must offer higher yields but use less water, nitrogen-rich fertilizers or other inputs.', '新优品种必须在实现超高产的同时，大幅缩减水资源消耗、显著减少富氮化肥及其他农化制剂的投放。'), ('Speaker', 'These new crops must also be more resistant to drought, heat and pests.', '这些新兴作物还必须具备抗旱、耐极端高温以及抗病虫害的卓越韧性。'), ('Speaker', 'Equally crucial is lower-tech research into basics such as crop rotation and mixed farming of animals and plants on small farms.', '同样关键的是针对基层小农场的实用型低技术基础研究，例如轮作套种机制以及动植物种养结合的复合循环农业。'), ('Speaker', 'Developing nations could score substantial gains in productivity by making better use of modern technologies and practices.', '发展中国家若能更加充分地消化运用现代农技与管理实践，完全能够在生产力上斩获跨越式突破。'), ('Speaker', 'But that requires money.', '但这一切都需要真金白银的巨额资金投入。'), ('Speaker', 'It is estimated that to meet the 2050 challenge, investment must double to 83 billion US dollars a year.', '据权威测算，要战胜2050年的粮食危机挑战，全球年均农业投资必须翻倍提升至830亿美元。'), ('Speaker', 'Most of that money needs to go towards improving agricultural infrastructure.', '其中绝大部分资金亟需投向农业基础设施的升级改造工程。'), ('Speaker', 'Everything from production to storage and processing must improve.', '从农田生产、仓储保鲜到深加工全产业链的每一个环节都必须全面升级换代。'), ('Speaker', 'However, research agendas need to be focused on the needs of the poorest and most resource-limited countries.', '与此同时，科研立项重心必须紧密聚焦于最贫困、资源最为匮乏的发展中国家的迫切需求。'), ('Speaker', "It is there that most of the world's population lives and it is there that population growth over the next decades will be the greatest.", '因为全球绝大多数人口正是繁衍生息在这些地区，且未来数十载的人口新增洪峰也必将集中爆发于此。'), ('Speaker', "To their credit, the world's agricultural scientists are embracing such a broad view.", '令人欣慰的是，全球杰出的农业科学家们正以非凡的担当拥抱这一全球宏阔大局。'), ('Speaker', 'In March, for example, they came together at the first Global Conference on Agricultural Research to begin working out how to change research agendas to help meet the needs of farmers in poorer nations.', '例如在三月份举行的首届全球农业研究大会上，科学家们济济一堂，共同研讨如何重塑科研课题以精准对接贫困国家广大农民的切实所需。'), ('Speaker', 'But these plans will not bear fruit unless they get considerably more support from policy-makers.', '但这些宏图壮志若想开花结果，必须获得各国决策层实质性、大力度政策扶持与资金倾斜。'), ('Speaker', 'The growth in public agricultural-research spending peaked in the 1970s and has been shrinking ever since.', '全球公共农业科研支出的增长在20世纪70年代触顶，此后数十年间便持续处于萎缩疲软状态。'), ('Speaker', 'The big exception is China, where spending has far surpassed other countries over the past decade.', '而在全球范围内最亮眼的例外正是中国——在过去的十年里，中国在农业科研领域的资金投入已遥遥领先于其他所有国家。'), ('Speaker', 'China seems set to transition to become the key supplier of relevant science and technology to poorer countries, but developed countries have a humanitarian responsibility too.', '中国正势不可挡地跃升为向广大贫困落后国家输出核心农业科技的关键供给国，但发达国家同样肩负着不可推卸的人道主义援助重任。'), ('Speaker', 'Calls by scientists for large increases in the appropriation of funds for public spending on agricultural research are more than justified.', '科学家们关于大幅追加公共财政预算对农业科研实施战略性拨款的强烈呼吁，不仅完全合理，更是势在必行。')]}]

QUESTIONS = {1: {'prompt': "What do we learn about the woman's new book?", 'options': {'A': 'It has given rise to much controversy.', 'B': 'It has been very favorably received.', 'C': 'It was primarily written for vegetarians.', 'D': 'It offends many environmentalists.'}, 'answer': 'A', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。主持人开场介绍嘉宾：“With me today is Meghan Brown, an environmental activist whose controversial new book Beyond Recycling is making headlines.”梅根·布朗极具争议性的新书《超越回收》成为新闻热点，引发了很大争议。因此答案为 A)。'}, 2: {'prompt': 'What do some critics say about the author of the book?', 'options': {'A': "She neglects people's efforts in animal protection.", 'B': 'She tries to force people to accept her radical ideas.', 'C': 'She ignores the various benefits of public transport.', 'D': 'She insists vegetarians are harming the environment.'}, 'answer': 'B', 'explanation': "【精析】细节辨认题。主持人在访谈中提及批评者观点：“Critics of your book assert that you're trying to force radical changes on the entire country. Some claim that you want to force everyone...”批评者声称作者试图强迫大家接受其激进主张（force radical changes）。因此答案为 B)。"}, 3: {'prompt': 'What does the woman claim about the diet changes she suggested?', 'options': {'A': 'They are significant.', 'B': 'They are revolutionary.', 'C': 'They are rational.', 'D': 'They are modest.'}, 'answer': 'D', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。女士澄清自己给公众的建议时强调：“In my guidelines for saving the environment, I suggest modest changes, like eating vegetarian meals two days a week.”她所提倡的是温和适度的改变（modest changes）。因此答案为 D)。'}, 4: {'prompt': 'What does the woman say about her suggested tax increase?', 'options': {'A': 'It would help to protect the environment.', 'B': 'It would generate money for public health.', 'C': 'It would need support from the general public.', 'D': 'It would force poor people to change their diet.'}, 'answer': 'A', 'explanation': '【精析】细节推断题。针对税收质疑，女士解释说增税不到3%：“Plus, the money generated would be allocated to environmental protection, which benefits everyone.”增税募集的资金将用于环境保护并惠及大众。因此答案为 A)。'}, 5: {'prompt': 'What has the woman revealed in her book?', 'options': {'A': "Where successful people's strengths come from.", 'B': 'Why many people fight so hard for success.', 'C': "How she achieved her life's goal.", 'D': 'What makes people successful.'}, 'answer': 'D', 'explanation': '【精析】细节推断题。主持人介绍新书时表示：“She claims to have uncovered how people achieve success.”洛根女士在新书中揭示了人们是如何走向成功、是什么让人们获得成功的（What makes people successful）。因此答案为 D)。'}, 6: {'prompt': 'What do successful people attribute their achievement to?', 'options': {'A': 'Having someone who has confidence in them.', 'B': 'Having someone who is ready to help them.', 'C': 'Having a firm belief in their own ability.', 'D': 'Having a realistic attitude towards life.'}, 'answer': 'A', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。洛根女士分析成功特质时指出：“They credit their success to having someone in their life who believes in them.”成功人士将自己的成就归功于生活中有人由衷信任他们。因此答案为 A)。'}, 7: {'prompt': 'What do successful people do when faced with difficulties?', 'options': {'A': 'They adjust their goals accordingly.', 'B': 'They try hard to appear optimistic.', 'C': 'They stay positive.', 'D': 'They remain calm.'}, 'answer': 'C', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。女士在谈到面对困难与阻碍时指出：“Successful people are also optimistic as it is important to stay positive while being aware of obstacles that can deter us from achieving our goals.”成功人士在清醒意识到障碍的同时始终保持积极心态（stay positive）。因此答案为 C)。'}, 8: {'prompt': 'What is one prerequisite for passion at work according to the woman?', 'options': {'A': 'An understanding leadership.', 'B': 'A nurturing environment.', 'C': 'Mutual respect among colleagues.', 'D': 'Highly cooperative teammates.'}, 'answer': 'B', 'explanation': "【精析】细节辨认题。谈及工作激情的产生机制，女士强调先决条件：“There's a prerequisite, that is, you have to work in an environment that nurtures passion.”必须身处一个能够滋养培育激情的环境之中（A nurturing environment）。因此答案为 B)。"}, 9: {'prompt': 'What do we learn about mega bats?', 'options': {'A': 'They use their sense of hearing to capture their prey.', 'B': 'Their food mainly consists of small animals and fish.', 'C': 'They have big eyes and distinctive visual centers.', 'D': 'Their ancestor is different from that of micro bats.'}, 'answer': 'C', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。短文详细介绍了大蝙蝠的生理特征：“These species have distinctive visual centers and big eyes. They use senses of vision and smell to capture their prey.”大蝙蝠长有大眼睛和独特的视觉中枢。因此答案为 C)。'}, 10: {'prompt': 'How do micro bats find their way and identify food?', 'options': {'A': 'With the help of moonlight.', 'B': 'By means of echolocation.', 'C': 'With the aid of daylight vision.', 'D': 'By means of vision and smell.'}, 'answer': 'B', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。短文介绍小蝙蝠时明确指出：“These species use echolocation to find their way and identify food.”微型小蝙蝠借助回声定位（echolocation）来引路导航和锁定食物。因此答案为 B)。'}, 11: {'prompt': 'Why do some species of bats use their sense of hearing more than their eyes?', 'options': {'A': 'To make up for their natural absence of vision.', 'B': 'To adapt themselves to a particular lifestyle.', 'C': 'To facilitate their travel over long distances.', 'D': 'To survive in the ever-changing weather.'}, 'answer': 'B', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。短文最后阐明其原因：“Some species use their sense of hearing more than their eyes as a matter of adaptation to a particular lifestyle.”部分蝠类侧重使用听觉是适应特定生活习性的进化结果。因此答案为 B)。'}, 12: {'prompt': 'What does the passage say about children watching educational programs?', 'options': {'A': 'They acquire knowledge not found in books.', 'B': 'They learn how to interact with their peers.', 'C': 'They become more emotionally aggressive.', 'D': 'They get much better prepared for school.'}, 'answer': 'C', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。研究表明：“Children spending more time watching educational programs increase their emotional aggression toward other children.”花更多时间看教育节目的孩子在情绪上往往更具攻击性（emotionally aggressive）。因此答案为 C)。'}, 13: {'prompt': "Why can't preschool children get the moral conveyed in the TV programs?", 'options': {'A': 'They are far from emotionally prepared.', 'B': 'They tend to be more attracted by images.', 'C': "They can't follow the conflicts in the show.", 'D': 'They lack the cognitive and memory skills.'}, 'answer': 'D', 'explanation': '【精析】细节推断题。针对幼童为何无法领悟寓意，短文解释：“You need pretty complicated cognitive skills and memory skills to be able to do that. These are still developing in young children.”幼儿尚未具备足以把控复杂情节所需的认知与记忆能力。因此答案为 D)。'}, 14: {'prompt': 'What does the passage suggest parents do?', 'options': {'A': 'Choose appropriate programs for their children.', 'B': "Help their children understand the program's plot.", 'C': "Outline the program's plot for their children first.", 'D': "Monitor their children's watching of TV programs."}, 'answer': 'B', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。短文建议父母：“Parents should instead watch with their kids and help them to understand the plot.”父母应当陪同观看并协助孩子理解剧情发展。因此答案为 B)。'}, 15: {'prompt': 'What should parents do right after watching the TV program?', 'options': {'A': 'Explain its message to their children.', 'B': 'Check if their children have enjoyed it.', 'C': 'Encourage their children to retell the story.', 'D': 'Ask their children to describe its characters.'}, 'answer': 'A', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。短文指出：“Parents can comment along the way and then explain the message at the end.”父母可以在观看结束时向孩子解析说明节目所传达的道德真谛。因此答案为 A)。'}, 16: {'prompt': "Why don't many Westerners take off shoes before entering a house?", 'options': {'A': 'They are afraid of injuring their feet.', 'B': 'They have never developed the habit.', 'C': 'They believe a little dirt harms no one.', 'D': 'They find it rather troublesome to do so.'}, 'answer': 'C', 'explanation': "【精析】细节辨认题。讲座开篇指出西方人不脱鞋进屋的心态：“After all, they may think a little dirt doesn't hurt anyone.”很多人认为一点点污垢尘土不会伤害到任何人。因此答案为 C)。"}, 17: {'prompt': 'What is the finding of one study by researchers at an American university?', 'options': {'A': 'Different types of bacteria existed on public-toilet floors.', 'B': 'There were more bacteria on sidewalks than in the home.', 'C': 'Office carpets collected more bacteria than elsewhere.', 'D': 'A large number of bacteria collected on a single shoe.'}, 'answer': 'D', 'explanation': '【精析】细节推断题。美国高校科学家的研究显示：“They found that up to 421,000 units of bacteria can collect on the outside of a single shoe.”仅单只鞋子外面就滋生集聚了高达42.1万个单位的大量细菌（A large number of bacteria）。因此答案为 D)。'}, 18: {'prompt': 'What is the final reason the speaker gives for removing shoes before entering a house?', 'options': {'A': 'The chemicals on shoes can deteriorate air quality.', 'B': 'Shoes can upset family members with their noise.', 'C': 'The marks left by shoes are hard to erase.', 'D': 'Shoes can leave scratches on the floor.'}, 'answer': 'A', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。讲话者给出的终极理由是：“The dust and toxic chemicals you bring into your house via your shoes can deteriorate the air quality in your home.”鞋底带进的有毒化学物质与粉尘会恶化居室内空气质量。因此答案为 A)。'}, 19: {'prompt': "What does the speaker say about hiding one's emotions?", 'options': {'A': 'It is sinful and immoral.', 'B': 'It is deemed uncivilized.', 'C': 'It is an uncontrollable behavior.', 'D': 'It is a violation of faith and trust.'}, 'answer': 'D', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。讲座中指出掩饰情感的伦理代价：“Socially, it may be a good tactic to hide our true emotions, but morally it is also a breach of faith and trust.”在道德层面上，隐瞒真实心声是对信任与诚信的背叛违背（violation of faith and trust）。因此答案为 D)。'}, 20: {'prompt': 'What should we do first in dealing with emotions?', 'options': {'A': 'Assess their consequences.', 'B': 'Guard against their harm.', 'C': 'Accept them as normal.', 'D': 'Find out their causes.'}, 'answer': 'C', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。讲座强调直面情绪的首要一步：“One of the first steps in dealing with emotions such as anger or fear is to acknowledge them as normal and human.”第一步是接纳情绪的自然正当性（Accept them as normal）。因此答案为 C)。'}, 21: {'prompt': 'What are we advised to do when emotions arise?', 'options': {'A': 'Try to understand what messages they convey.', 'B': 'Pay attention to their possible consequences.', 'C': 'Consider them from different perspectives.', 'D': 'Make sure they are brought under control.'}, 'answer': 'A', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。面对汹涌情绪，讲话者建议：“When emotions arise, instead of stifling them, pay attention to them and try to understand the messages they are trying to deliver.”不要一味压抑，而要倾听并理解情绪试图传递的内在信号。因此答案为 A)。'}, 22: {'prompt': "What is an urgent need for feeding the world's population in 2050, according to the speaker?", 'options': {'A': 'Cultivation of new varieties of crops.', 'B': 'Measures to cope with climate change.', 'C': 'Development of more effective pesticides.', 'D': 'Application of more nitrogen-rich fertilizers.'}, 'answer': 'A', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。演讲者指出完成2050年全球人口粮食供给的当务之急：“There is an urgent need for new crop varieties. They must offer higher yields but use less water...”必须抓紧培育高产少肥抗逆的农作物新品种（Cultivation of new varieties of crops）。因此答案为 A)。'}, 23: {'prompt': 'Where should most of the money be invested to feed the ever-growing population?', 'options': {'A': 'The expansion of farmland in developing countries.', 'B': 'The research on crop rotation in developing countries.', 'C': "The cooperation of the world's agricultural scientists.", 'D': 'The improvement of agricultural infrastructure.'}, 'answer': 'D', 'explanation': '【精析】细节辨认题。在论及新增资金流向时，讲话明确强调：“Most of that money needs to go towards improving agricultural infrastructure.”大部分资金必须注入农业基础设施的改良升级中。因此答案为 D)。'}, 24: {'prompt': "Why does the speaker give credit to the world's agricultural scientists?", 'options': {'A': 'For encouraging farmers to embrace new farming techniques.', 'B': 'For aligning their research with advances in farming technology.', 'C': 'For turning their focus to the needs of farmers in poorer countries.', 'D': 'For cooperating closely with policymakers in developing countries.'}, 'answer': 'C', 'explanation': "【精析】细节辨认题。讲话赞扬全球农业科学家的宏阔胸襟：“To their credit, the world's agricultural scientists... begin working out how to change research agendas to help meet the needs of farmers in poorer nations.”科学家们主动将科研聚焦点转向最贫困国家农户的迫切需求。因此答案为 C)。"}, 25: {'prompt': 'What makes China exceptional in comparison with the rest of the world?', 'options': {'A': 'Rapid transition to become a food exporter.', 'B': 'Substantial funding in agricultural research.', 'C': 'Quick rise to become a leading grain producer.', 'D': 'Assumption of humanitarian responsibilities.'}, 'answer': 'B', 'explanation': '【精析】细节推断题。讲话对比了全球公共农业支出萎缩的现状并指出：“The big exception is China, where spending has far surpassed other countries over the past decade.”中国在农业前沿科研领域的巨额财政经费投入大幅超越其他所有国家。因此答案为 B)。'}}
